        "code": "// A caller that OMITS a field entirely - rather than sending \"\" - must get a\n// business outcome, not \"No such property\". An unbound parameter is not a null\n// variable in Groovy; it is a missing one, so it has to be asked for by name.\ndef raw = { n -> binding.hasVariable(n) ? binding.getVariable(n) : null }\ndef t = { v -> v == null ? '' : v.toString().trim() }\ndef s  = t(raw('search'))\ndef mr = t(raw('maxRows'))\n\nboolean valid = true\nString reason = ''\n\n// THE WHOLE CATALOG, ALWAYS. This is an export, not a page of the screen - the\n// caller's own paging is deliberately ignored, and there is no offset. The\n// ceiling is a runaway guard, not a page size: nothing clamps `page.limit` on the\n// way through (BaseStorageAction.getPageDetailsOrDefault passes it straight to the\n// query), so one fetch really does return everything a realistic catalog holds.\n// If it is ever hit, the run says TRUNCATED rather than handing back a short file.\nint rowCap = 50000\nif (!mr.isEmpty()) {\n    if (mr ==~ /^\\d+$/) { rowCap = Integer.parseInt(mr) } else { valid = false; reason = 'maxRows must be a whole number, got: ' + mr }\n}\nif (rowCap < 1) rowCap = 1\nif (rowCap > 50000) rowCap = 50000\n\n// The SAME OR-search ICM | Manage Titles uses for LIST. Left blank by the Download\n// button, which wants the whole catalog; supported so a caller that wants the file\n// to match a filtered screen can ask for exactly that.\ndef lf = []\nif (!valid) {\n    lf << [property: 'id', filter: [operator: 'EQUAL', value: '__invalid_input__']]\n} else if (!s.isEmpty()) {\n    lf << [operator: 'OR', filters: [\n        [property: 'properties.titleCode',   filter: [operator: 'ICONTAINS', value: s]],\n        [property: 'properties.name',        filter: [operator: 'ICONTAINS', value: s]],\n        [property: 'properties.description', filter: [operator: 'ICONTAINS', value: s]]]]\n}\n\nreturn [valid: valid, reason: reason, search: s, rowCap: rowCap,\n        listFilter: [operator: 'AND', filters: lf]]\n",
        "compile_static": false,
        "captureStdOutput": false,
        "parameters": {
